-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1116. two-traces.l4 with an `#EVAL `taken now`` in place of
-- the first trace: the #EVAL reads the imported rule against an empty ledger,
-- and the skip trace after it must still read it against its own, as it does
-- alone (one COMMIT, WITHIN 9).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT taken

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Bob
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF peek, skip
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    go HAS mode IS A Mode
    buy

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`shop` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY buy PROVIDED NOT `taken now`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS TRUE HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`start` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY go m
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS (IF m EQUALS peek THEN NOT `taken now` ELSE TRUE) HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

#EVAL `taken now`

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go skip AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2
